# tools/g/gitlink_dependent_witness.rish -- a guard that reds on a dependency a correct clone may
# lack can never be rostered, so its refusal is one nobody will ever hear.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/g/gitlink_dependent_witness.rish
#
# THE TWO ROOMS. This tree holds twelve gitlinks. `vendor/` holds what the tree LINKS, and the
# operator card names its four rungs a precondition every clone initialises -- a red from an empty
# one is an environment fact. `gratitude/` holds a READING LIBRARY the gratitude-licenses law says we
# study and never copy, so a clone that never initialised `gratitude/tigerbeetle` is a CORRECT clone.
#
# WHAT THIS COUNTS, and why it is a count rather than a sample. REDS %646 found the shape by
# sampling 40 of the unreached witnesses -- 35 green, 5 red -- and among the five were preconditions.
# Its lesson: a hard assert on an optional precondition buys a red nobody hears, because it makes the
# witness unrostable and an unrostered witness runs nowhere. The row closed one witness as a worked
# example and left the class as *a sweep whose size is the sample rather than a count*. Counted here
# on `20260908.214427`: 22 dependents, every one in the tigerbeetle census family, against 32 that
# depend on a required `vendor/` rung and are covered by the card already.
#
# THAT FIGURE IS FREE, and it has already moved. `20260908.224618` drew the sixth probe --
# `capability tigerbeetle_clone` -- and rostered one of the 22 behind it, so the population reads 21
# and falls with every further rostering. Read `optional_unrostered` off the scan rather than off
# this paragraph: a witness header reciting a number its own scan derives is the drift the standing
# equipment witness confessed to one room over, where a header said `forty-three` while the control
# ran more.
#
# AND THE POPULATION WAS NAMED FOR A BEHAVIOR NOBODY HAD RUN (`20260911`). The reading was static:
# it counted a runner naming an optional gitlink on a working line with no roster row, called that
# `optional_unrostable`, and said of each member *reds when an optional submodule is absent*. Run
# with `gratitude/tigerbeetle` empty -- how every ship on this pier stands -- **38 of 38 exit 0**,
# each printing an honest SKIP, the whole population in 768 ms. Not one reds. The count was a count
# of a SHAPE and the sentence claimed a BEHAVIOR, and the two are different populations; the reading
# is named `optional_unrostered` from here, which is what it reads.
#
# So the scan grew a `probe` mode that RUNS each optional dependent whose gitlinks stand empty and
# classifies it by exit status, and this witness asks for that mode rather than the static one. The
# second gate, `probe_red=0`, is what turns REDS %646's 5-in-40 sample into a wall: a runner written
# with a hard assert over a reading library reds on the lap it lands.
#
# THE CURE ALREADY STANDS, which is the second finding and the larger one. REDS %460, one lane over,
# named the roster's `capability` field as the mechanism for exactly this and called seating it a
# design act awaiting a word. That field was built `20260829` and carried five probes when this was
# written -- six from `20260908.224618`, the sixth drawn for this very family -- two of
# which -- `seed_projection` and `day_shelf` -- answer this same question about a different absent
# thing. So the two open rows are one gate, and the gate has a door.
#
# THE GATE IS THE ONE ROW THAT WOULD RED THE FLEET: a rostered guard depending on an optional
# gitlink and naming no capability. Held at zero, beside `probe_red`. The unrostered population is reported rather than
# gated, because rostering a study census is a hand's decision with a probe attached, and a guard
# that reds on a decision nobody has made is a guard somebody turns off.

say "gitlink-dependent: Language EN -- what a correct clone may lack, and who reds over it."
say "gitlink-dependent: Style Gauge, Meter -- two gates at zero, one population reported."
say "gitlink-dependent: Lens TAME -- every refusal planted and then lifted."

say "gitlink-dependent: the control -- thirty-seven behaviors on real repositories in a throwaway pen..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/g/gitlink_dependent_control.sh"]
assert ctl.ok else "gitlink-dependent: the control refused --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"
assert ctl.out contains "pass=37 fail=0" else "gitlink-dependent: the control did not prove thirty-seven behaviors --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"

say "gitlink-dependent: and this tree's own reading..."
let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/g/gitlink_dependent_scan.sh" "probe"]
# invariant: a refusal reports BOTH streams, since this scan writes its reason to stderr and the
# reds file a reader opens would otherwise carry an empty line where the reason belongs.
assert scan.ok else "gitlink-dependent: the scan refused --\n${scan.out}\n${scan.err}"
# invariant: the gate is held at zero -- a rostered guard whose refusal depends on a submodule a
# correct clone may lack would red every machine in the fleet that studies rather than clones.
assert scan.out contains "rostered_undeclared=0" else "gitlink-dependent: a rostered guard depends on an optional submodule and names no capability --\n${scan.out}"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "gitlink-dependent: the census refused --\n${scan.out}\n${scan.err}"
# invariant: both populations are reported, empty or full. A reading that printed only the fault
# would leave a reader unable to tell a healthy tree from a scan that could not see one.
assert scan.out contains "optional_unrostered=" else "gitlink-dependent: the unrostered population went unreported"
# invariant: the probe gate is held at zero -- a runner that REFUSES over a reading library a
# correct clone may lack is REDS %646's shape exactly, and this is where it reds on arrival.
assert scan.out contains "probe_red=0" else "gitlink-dependent: an optional dependent refuses over an absent reading library --\n${scan.out}"
# invariant: the measured readings are all three reported, empty or full, so a reader tells a clean
# population from a probe that could see nothing. `probe_unread` is the honest zero here: every
# gratitude gitlink on this pier stands empty, so every dependent was actually run.
assert scan.out contains "probe_green=" else "gitlink-dependent: the probe reported no green count"
assert scan.out contains "probe_unread=" else "gitlink-dependent: the probe reported no unread count"
assert scan.out contains "required_dependents=" else "gitlink-dependent: the required population went unreported"
assert scan.out contains "optional_gitlinks=" else "gitlink-dependent: the two rooms were not counted apart"
# The closing line tells a reader to READ `optional_unrostered` above, and until `20260911` nothing
# here printed it -- the scan's whole output stood captured in `scan.out` and was said nowhere. A
# guard pointing at a line it never speaks is the same fault this lap came to repair, one room in.
# BARE, never interpolated (`rish_report_bound`, repaired `20260911.035245` as this lap landed out of
# a stash): `say "${scan.out}"` opens a 4096-byte StrBuf and would end the run on a GREEN reading
# once this census outgrew it. A bare `say` writes the value straight out, as `reds_spine_derive` does.
say scan.out

say "gitlink-dependent: and the capability field the cure rests on is really built..."
# invariant: the roster honors at least one capability probe. This witness recommends a mechanism to
# whoever reads the unrostered population, and recommending one the runner does not implement would
# be prose rather than a door.
let caps = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -c '^capability ' construction/standing-equipment.kyri || true"]
assert caps.ok else "gitlink-dependent: the roster could not be read"
assert (trim caps.out) != "0" else "gitlink-dependent: the capability field this reading points at is named by no roster row"

# The closing line names the READING rather than a figure. The elder spelled `22`, which was true
# for six hours and false the moment the first dependent was rostered behind a probe -- and a GREEN
# line carrying a stale number is worse than one carrying none, since it is read as measurement.
# The scan's own `optional_unrostered=` line is said above and is the record.
say "GREEN: gitlink-dependent -- the unrostered population counted rather than sampled (read `optional_unrostered` above), zero rostered undeclared, zero refusing over an absent reading library when actually RUN (`probe_red`), and the capability door proven open and walked through."
